<title>GERMANY: Mercedes pact to preserve Sindelfingen jobs.</title>
<headline>Mercedes pact to preserve Sindelfingen jobs.</headline>
<dateline>STUTTGART, Germany 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The works council and management of Mercedes-Benz AG's Sindelfingen plant have reached an agreement to preserve jobs at the factory, Mercedes said in a statement.</p>
<p>The spokesman said as part of the deal, the works council had agreed that models to replace the C- and E-Class cars will be made at the car plant, Mercedes' largest.</p>
<p>Around 35,000 workers are employed at the plant. Mercedes is the car and truck making unit of Daimler-Benz AG.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom + 49 69 756525</p>
